# DS5005: two columns where one is expected.
mode: check
schema: t(customerId: string, month: datetime, revenue: real, n: long)
---- query
from t
| render piechart with (xcolumn = customerId, month, ycolumns = revenue, n)
---- expected
error[DS5005]: `xcolumn` takes one column
  --> query:2:47
  |
2 | | render piechart with (xcolumn = customerId, month, ycolumns = revenue, n)
  |                                               ^^^^^ a chart has one x-axis
  |
  = help: remove the extra columns

error[DS5005]: a `piechart` takes one column in `ycolumns`
  --> query:2:74
  |
2 | | render piechart with (xcolumn = customerId, month, ycolumns = revenue, n)
  |                                                                          ^ a pie chart has one value per slice
  |
  = help: remove the extra columns
